10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Kids is a 1995 American independent coming-of-age drama film directed by Larry Clark and written
by Harmony Korine in their directorial and screenwriting debuts, respectively.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
It stars Leo Fitzpatrick, Justin Pierce and Chloë Sevigny in their film debuts.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Fitzpatrick, Pierce, Sevigny, and other newcomers including Rosario
Dawson portray a group of teenagers in New York City.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
They are characterized as libertines, who engage in sexual acts and
recreational substance abuse, over the course of a single day.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Ben Detrick of the New York Times has described the film as "Lord of
the Flies with skateboards, nitrous oxide and hip-hop...

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
There is no thunderous moral reckoning, only observational detachment." The film caused
controversy upon its release in 1995 over its treatment of the subject matter.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It received an NC-17 rating from the MPAA, but was released without a rating.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Critical response was mixed, and the film grossed
$20.4 million on a $1.5 million budget.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It is now considered a cult classic.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film explores themes of puberty, first time, new
york city, drug abuse, coming of age.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
